From: broody <broody@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 11:12:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Bounded-memory storage for the PROOF2 large path (Cairo
 leaf and verifier circuit)

prove_cairo_bounded, prove_leaf_bounded and privacy_recursive_prove_large_bounded
take an optional FRI column batch per stage and select the ported
coefficient-backed PCS mode; the existing functions are unchanged (None).
The bounded Cairo preprocessed tree keeps coefficients so it can be evicted.
prove_leaf drops the Cairo VM runner after the adapter. prove_large reads
TEMPLAR_BOUNDED_CAIRO_COLUMNS / TEMPLAR_BOUNDED_CIRCUIT_COLUMNS and, with
TEMPLAR_SPAN_EVENTS=1, logs span closes for stage timing.

Storage policy only: proofs are byte-identical to the default path and
verify with the V2 verifier.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
